From e04cf9f829b78a59b20e00945c3a3b2375efed34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:29:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(xtask): the heavy reach reads test-only and
 binary-only source files

A changed #[cfg(test)] module of a heavy crate now reaches only that
crate's lib target, and src/main.rs or src/bin/.. reaches only the bins
and integration binaries of its crate. Every other file, and every file
the module walk cannot prove, keeps the crate reach. The plan names each
heavy step it does not run and prints the reached and skipped counts.

The per-module use graph for library files is not in this change: it
needs guards for globs, re-exports, trait impls and registries.

Refs #3560

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
