From d1eb8402018c2c394d46ee8d98fe2cfa50e7917c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:10:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(xtask): a test-only file is narrow only when no other
 compile root names it

Review of #3737: the cfg(test) proof read only the lib.rs module tree.
A `mod t;` in main.rs, or a `#[path]` in tests/ or src/bin, could build
the same file into another target. seen_by now reads every .rs file of
the crate directory and answers Library when any of them names the file
or declares one of its modules outside the proven tree. heavy.rs and
heavy_files_tests.rs are LF again, as on main.

Refs #3560

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
